INT. POLAR STATION HALLEY-9, MEDICAL BAY - NIGHT

A cramped clinic: one exam bed, one monitor, one satellite screen glowing blue on the wall. Wind howls at the walls.

DR. SUNNIVA ERIKSEN, 40s, the station physician, stands at the screen with her arms crossed. IBRAHIM TARAWNEH, 30s, a mechanic, sits on the bed with a bandaged hand and a gray face.

                    SUNNIVA
          Dr. Lakshmi, can you hear me?

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          I can. Go ahead, Sunniva. Describe the wound.

                    SUNNIVA
          Laceration across the palm, six centimeters. Clean edges. He's been bleeding for an hour.

                    IBRAHIM
          It's fine.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Mr. Tarawneh, I need you to keep your hand elevated.

                    IBRAHIM
          It's elevated.

                    SUNNIVA
          It's on your knee.

                    IBRAHIM
          I'm resting it on my knee.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Sunniva, what's his heart rate?

                    SUNNIVA
          One-ten. Pressure ninety over sixty.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          That's low for a hand wound.

                    IBRAHIM
          I'm cold.

                    SUNNIVA
          You're not cold, you're pale.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Mr. Tarawneh, how did you cut it?

                    IBRAHIM
          Generator. A panel slipped.

                    SUNNIVA
          That's not what you told me.

                    IBRAHIM
          It's what happened.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Ibrahim, I'm going to ask you directly. Did you take anything for the pain?

                    IBRAHIM
          No.

                    SUNNIVA
          Ibrahim.

                    IBRAHIM
          A few of the white ones. Maybe six.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Six what?

                    SUNNIVA
          Oxycodone. The stock bottle. It's empty.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          The stock bottle held sixty tablets.

                    IBRAHIM
          I had a long winter.

                    SUNNIVA
          Ibrahim, how many?

                    IBRAHIM
          All of them. Since October.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          Sunniva, this is no longer a hand injury.

                    SUNNIVA
          I know.

                    IBRAHIM
          Please don't tell the crew.

                    LAKSHMI (V.O.)
          We will talk about that after we keep you alive.
